    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28869" root="عرن" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَارِنٌ</span></b> : see its fem., with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِرَانٌ</span>, last sentence but one, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العَارِنُ</span> <i>The lion:</i>
(K:) [app. a possessive epithet, meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذُو</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العَرِينِ</span>: but he is said to be thus called] because
of his abominable nature, and his strength. (TA.)

